module

public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.DerivedHomComplete
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Pushforward
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Both sides of the formal-functions comparison are derived complete

Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed sites, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` and `ℐ' ⊂ 𝒪'` be
sheaves of ideals such that `f^♯` sends `f^{-1}ℐ` into `ℐ'`, and let `K` be an object of `D(𝒪')`.
[Stacks, Tag 0A0I] is the displayed equation

`Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧`

of the section on the theorem on formal functions: derived direct image commutes with derived
completion. [Stacks, Tag 0AKL] is the remark that closes that section, and the analogue of the
displayed equation *for complexes of quasi-coherent modules* which its last sentence attributes
to [HL-P, Theorem 6.5] is the subject of this file.

## Main results

The two objects the analogue compares are both of the shape "derived internal Hom into a
derived-complete object, pushed forward" or "pushed forward, then derived internal Hom into".
Both are derived complete along `ℐ` as soon as `K` is derived complete along `ℐ'`:

* `isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedSheafHom`:
  `Rf_*(R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪'}(M, K))` is derived complete along `ℐ`, for every `M` in `D(𝒪')`.
* `isDerivedComplete_derivedSheafHom_derivedPushforward`:
  `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(N, Rf_*K)` is derived complete along `ℐ`, for every `N` in `D(𝒪)`.

[Stacks, Tag 099B] builds the derived completion as `K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom(Č(f_1, …, f_r), K)`, derived
internal Hom out of the extended alternating Čech complex of a finite family of global sections
generating the ideal — this is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor`. Instantiating `M`
at `Č` on the source and `N` at `Č` on the target therefore reads the two results as: *both sides
of the displayed equation of Tag 0A0I lie in `D_comp`*. That is the first step of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0G], the lemma Tag 0A0I makes explicit, and it is the step that makes the
comparison map between the two sides canonical.

The comparison isomorphism `Rf_*(K^∧) ≅ (Rf_*K)^∧` itself, at a morphism of schemes, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_forall_isNilpotent`
(local sections of both ideal sheaves nilpotent) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme`
`.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isDerivedComplete`
(a derived-complete object, ideal sheaves generated by finitely many global sections).

## Implementation notes

The source object of the derived internal Hom is left arbitrary rather than fixed at the Čech
complex; the Čech complex is one value of `M`.

No quasi-coherence hypothesis is imposed: the coefficient `K` is an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪')`,
which subsumes the complexes of quasi-coherent modules of [HL-P, Theorem 6.5]. Tag 0A0I itself has
a single quasi-coherent *sheaf* as its coefficient.

The hypotheses, the universe collapse `RingedSite.{u, u, u}` and the spelling of the
compatibility of the two ideal sheaves are those of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete`, the formalisation of
[Stacks, Tag 099J], so that the two results compose with no transport.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AKL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AKL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunction

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

variable {X Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u}} (f : RingedSite.Hom X Y)

/-- **The pushed-forward completion is derived complete.** Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be
a morphism of ringed sites and let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`, `ℐ' ⊂ 𝒪'` be sheaves of ideals such that `f^♯` sends
`f^{-1}ℐ` into `ℐ'`. If `K` in `D(𝒪')` is derived complete along `ℐ'`, then for every `M` in
`D(𝒪')` the object `Rf_*(R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪'}(M, K))` is derived complete along `ℐ`.

Taking `M` to be the extended alternating Čech complex of a finite family of global sections
generating `ℐ'`, so that `R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪'}(M, K)` is the derived completion `K^∧` of
[Stacks, Tag 099B], this says that the left-hand side `Rf_*(K^∧)` of the displayed equation of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0I] is derived complete.

[Stacks, Tag 099A] puts `R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪'}(M, K)` in `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ')`, and [Stacks, Tag 099J]
carries it from there into `D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)`. -/
@[stacks 0AKL "the mathematical content of the remark, which is its fifth and last sentence:
  the analogue of the displayed equation (0A0I) for complexes of quasi-coherent modules,
  [HL-P, Theorem 6.5]. The first four sentences are bibliography and carry no mathematical
  statement — a pointer to [lurie-thesis, Theorem 6.3.1] for a derived formal functions theorem
  for proper maps, one to [dag12, Chapter 4] together with the cross-reference to More on
  Algebra, Section 091N for the affine story, and one to [G-R, Section 2.9] for proper base
  change and derived completion via (ind) coherent modules. Covered here and in
  `isDerivedComplete_derivedSheafHom_derivedPushforward`: that both sides of (0A0I) are derived
  complete, for an arbitrary coefficient object of the derived category of modules, which
  subsumes the complexes of quasi-coherent modules the sentence speaks of. This is the step of
  the proof of Tag 0A0G that makes the comparison between the two sides canonical. NOT covered:
  the comparison isomorphism itself, which cannot be stated while Tag 099B and Tag 099F leave
  the derived completion without the universal property that pins the map down, nor proved
  while Tag 0944 and Tag 0A0E are unavailable; and not the setting of (derived) algebraic
  stacks in which [HL-P, Theorem 6.5] is stated. See the module documentation."]
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedSheafHom
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))))
    (I' : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hI : ∀ (W : Y.C) (s : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).obj.obj (op W)),
      s ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op W) →
        fSharpSection f W s ∈ I'.toSubmodule.obj (op (f.u.obj W)))
    (M K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I' K) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} Y I
      ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj
        (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op M)).obj K)) :=
  derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete f I I' hI _
    (isDerivedComplete_derivedSheafHom X I' M K hK)

/-- **The completion of a pushforward is derived complete.** In the situation of
`isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedSheafHom`, for every `N` in `D(𝒪)` the object
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(N, Rf_*K)` is derived complete along `ℐ`.

Taking `N` to be the extended alternating Čech complex of a finite family of global sections
generating `ℐ`, this says that the right-hand side `(Rf_*K)^∧` of the displayed equation of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0I] is derived complete.

The two inputs are used in the opposite order to the companion result: [Stacks, Tag 099J] puts
`Rf_*K` in `D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)` and [Stacks, Tag 099A] keeps the derived internal Hom into it there. -/
@[stacks 0AKL "the second half of the covered statement; see
  `isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedSheafHom` for the full accounting of which
  sentences of the remark carry mathematical content and of what is and is not covered."]
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedSheafHom_derivedPushforward
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))))
    (I' : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hI : ∀ (W : Y.C) (s : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).obj.obj (op W)),
      s ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op W) →
        fSharpSection f W s ∈ I'.toSubmodule.obj (op (f.u.obj W)))
    (N : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))))
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I' K) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} Y I
      (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor Y).obj (op N)).obj
        ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K)) :=
  isDerivedComplete_derivedSheafHom Y I N _
    (derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete f I I' hI K hK)

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
